# HTTP route schema

Google docstrings are for developers. `custom_route` does not generate an OpenAPI
document, so a docstring must not be treated as customer-facing copy.

`custom_route` is called only inside `http_routes/register_<feature>.py`. See
`registrator-funcs.mdc`. Pass `name=` and `include_in_schema=` to `mcp.custom_route`.
`name=` is what `get_http_route_logger` copies into the log `context`. Public response
bodies stay small JSON objects. Do not mention DI, loggers, or kubelet rationale
in a response body.

`FastMCP(version=)` is `installed_app_version()`, not `ENV`.

Probes stay registered; `include_in_schema` only when `ENV` is `local` or `dev`.
`/metrics` stays off the schema always.

An MCP tool, resource, or prompt passes `description=`. That string is what the
client lists. Omitting it publishes the docstring. Also pass `title`. A tool
that writes passes `annotations`. A resource whose body is JSON passes
`mime_type`. The docstring stays for developers, including implementation notes
that must not reach the client.
